# The root is where trying something out happens: a loose program, whatever it
# was compiled to, the log it was asked to write.  None of that has a settled
# name, and two such files were committed by a careless `git add -A` before this
# said so -- so what the root holds is listed rather than guessed at, and
# anything else there is ignored.  A file that belongs at the root is added
# here, which is one line and a deliberate act.
/*
!/*/
!/.gitignore
!/CLAUDE.md
!/TODO-language.md
!/TODO-pypl4g.md
!/pyproject.toml

# What a build leaves, anywhere.  These come after the rule above because the
# last one that matches is the one that holds, and the directories among them
# are ones that rule has just let back in.
build
*.o
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.core
*.log
